cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  DataForge: A Streaming, Leak-Aware Pipeline for Synthetic
  LLM Fine-Tuning Datasets
message: >-
  If you use this software or refer to this work, please cite
  the technical note below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ian K.
    family-names: Too
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0000-4888-1941'
    affiliation: William Jessup University
repository-code: 'https://github.com/ianktoo/data-forge'
version: 2.4.3
date-released: '2026-09-22'
abstract: >-
  DataForge is an open-source pipeline for building synthetic
  instruction-tuning datasets from websites. It honors HTTP
  failure semantics and robots.txt Crawl-delay during
  collection, checkpoints every artifact so long runs are
  resumable, overlaps collection and generation through
  bounded queues, bounds unattended LLM spend with an explicit
  budget, and performs group-aware train/test splitting so
  samples generated from the same source page cannot appear on
  both sides of a split and inflate held-out evaluation
  scores.
keywords:
  - synthetic data generation
  - instruction tuning
  - dataset construction
  - data leakage
  - group-aware splitting
  - LLM-as-judge
  - web scraping
  - Model Context Protocol
  - large language models
